# Prettier honours .gitignore by default only for files git already ignores;
# everything else below is content Prettier must not touch.

# Captured pages, verbatim.
#
# The scrape fixtures are byte-for-byte copies of what LinkedIn, Indeed and
# Naukri actually served. Reformatting them would rewrite the evidence: the
# suites assert exact card counts and an exact description length (2396
# characters), and re-indenting the HTML changes both. A fixture that has been
# prettified is no longer a capture — it is a guess about what the site sends.
packages/providers/src/scrape/__fixtures__/

# Build output and generated declarations.
dist/
dist-types/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Runtime data: the SQLite database, uploaded resumes, generated exports.
data/
mobile-site/jobs.json
mobile-site/admin.enc.json

# Dependencies.
node_modules/

# Lockfile — npm owns its formatting.
package-lock.json

# Scratch from the browser MCP tools during an interactive debugging session.
.playwright-mcp/
playwright-report/
test-results/

infra/nginx/*.inc
